    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">18(R)-RvE1, E2 and E3 translocate from cytosol to extracellular region</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref182" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref183" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">To produce their pro-resolving effects, 18(R)-RvE1, E2 and E3 are released into the exudate of local inflammation sites (Serhan et al. 2000). The mechanism of translocation is unknown.</bp:comment>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref2" />
